<section class="welcome-row"><div><span class="eyebrow">PROJECT INFORMATION</span><h1>About the project</h1><p>A practical digital foundation for a connected campus library.</p></div></section>
<section class="about-hero panel"><div class="about-wordmark"><span class="brand-mark">AU</span><div><strong>ALLIANCE UNIVERSITY</strong><small>SMART LIBRARY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM</small></div></div><h2>Better access.<br><span>Stronger discovery.</span></h2><p>Built to support librarians and students through accurate circulation, real-time availability, and useful library insights.</p></section>
<section class="about-cards"><article class="panel"><span class="eyebrow">PURPOSE</span><h2>What it does</h2><p>Manage the collection, student records, issue and return transactions, overdue fines, and reporting through a protected staff website.</p></article><article class="panel"><span class="eyebrow">TECHNOLOGY</span><h2>How it is built</h2><p>Java 17, JSP, Jakarta Servlets, JDBC, MySQL for production, H2 for local development, and Apache Tomcat 10.1. Interface, business logic, data access, and persistence are separated by responsibility.</p></article><article class="panel"><span class="eyebrow">ACADEMIC PROJECT</span><h2>Learning outcomes</h2><p>The project demonstrates object-oriented Java, role-based staff access, relational database design, transactions, validation, and responsive website design.</p></article></section>
